# Golden files are byte-exact fixtures: the test compares them against what the
# renderer produced in memory, which always uses LF. A CRLF checkout — the
# default on Windows, including the windows-latest CI runner — makes every line
# differ by an invisible trailing \r, and the failure reads as two identical
# lines that refuse to match.
*.golden text eol=lf

# The repository stores LF, but a Windows checkout under the default
# core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the working tree, and golangci-lint then
# reports files as unformatted against a diff no editor will show — a failure
# that does not exist on CI and costs an afternoon to disbelieve. Pinning eol
# makes the checkout match what the formatter expects.
*.go   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
